# Gemma 3 12B tuned for the stock-scoring pipeline.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Pulling `gemma3:12b` straight from Ollama uses Ollama's small default context window.
# The Fundamental agent's prompt is ~8k tokens (system prompt + evidence), so with the default
# window the prompt is SILENTLY TRUNCATED and the model scores on partial data. Baking a larger
# num_ctx into a named model (the same trick the existing `...-16k` qwen build uses) prevents that.
#
# BUILD:
#   ollama pull gemma3:12b
#   ollama create gemma3-12b-16k -f app/config/ollama/gemma3-12b-16k.Modelfile
#   ollama list            # confirm gemma3-12b-16k appears
#
# model_config.json already points the agents at "gemma3-12b-16k".
#
# VRAM NOTE: 12B (q4) ~8 GB of weights + KV cache. 16k context KV cache is a few GB more.
# If you are tight on memory, drop num_ctx to 12288 (prompts still fit) rather than running at the
# default — a truncated prompt is worse than a slightly smaller window.

FROM gemma3:12b

# Large enough to hold the biggest agent prompt plus its JSON answer without truncation.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

# Deterministic, analytical scoring. The decision_maker overrides to 0.0 via model_config.json/the API.
PARAMETER temperature 0.1

# Cap generation; agent replies are small JSON objects.
PARAMETER num_predict 2000
